"""The survey and settlement layer (Europe's point of view only).

Journeys alone cannot capture how much of the world was mapped by systematic survey, settlement and colonial administration.
These entries light whole regions (Natural Earth first-level divisions, by ISO 3166-2 code, or countries, by ISO alpha-3
code, optionally clipped to a box lon0, lat0, lon1, lat1) from the year the region's systematic survey or general mapping
was published in Europe or its settler colonisation was general. They are a separate layer ("survey") in the data and the
page; every result is also given for journeys alone.

Dates are from general knowledge of the history of cartography and settlement; the cited pages were not read for this
layer, so every entry carries the source status "years_not_confirmed". They are deliberately coarse: a region lights in one
year, and many areas (the Amazon, northern Siberia, the Sahara, interior Arabia, central Africa) are left to the journeys.
"""
W = "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/"
US = lambda *s: ["US-" + x for x in s]
